WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.240
We will spend the next several topics going&nbsp;
through some pretty typical situations we see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.720
in queries. For the first few situations,&nbsp;
the starting point will be this query,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.920
which lists people and their&nbsp;
addresses. I will execute this as is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:23.440
and we have a solid list, but what if we&nbsp;
want to sort the list? The ORDER BY clause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:32.480
is used to sort information. At the end of&nbsp;
the query, I will type ORDER BY LastName&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:41.280
to sort this on the last name column. I&nbsp;
will execute this statement, and now this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:48.080
alphabetical by LastName. We only need one ORDER&nbsp;
BY clause for multiple columns in a sort. I will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:57.760
add FirstName and then execute this again, and now&nbsp;
this is sorted by LastName and then by FirstName.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.960
To sort a column in descending order, we&nbsp;
just need to add the letters DECS at the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.760
of whichever column we want in descending&nbsp;
order, which will be the LastName field.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:17.520
I will execute this again, and now we have the&nbsp;
last names sorted alphabetically from Z to A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:24.240
and then within each last name,&nbsp;
by first name from A to Z.

